here we are on the 17th of march  and just a year ago  march 18 2020 one  year ago tomorrow i stood before you  to express my deepest concerns about  completely shutting down our beloved las  vegas  its hotels its businesses and its  schools  the decision by one individual which  required  no vote by the nevada legislature or any  other  elected body promised to cause  undue hardship to hundreds of thousands  of nevadans my plea at the time  was to take a more nuanced approach  to enact safety precautions that  would enable las vegas to continue to  function  a full year later we see some states  which took this moderate approach like  more populous  florida and texas for example  actually real realized a lower  death count per hundred thousand than  did some states with prolonged total  shutdowns  like michigan new york and nevada  and that's according to statista.com  march 8 2021  nevadans many of whom still have not  been able to get through to the state's  unemployment office to receive funds  owed to them suffered tremendously  many of our small businesses and even  some of our larger ones were forced to  close up  to shutter their doors and our children  have suffered immeasurably  as i pleaded for moderation some  individuals  especially some certain newscasters  took great issue with my stance to enact  reasonable safety precautions and  entrust  nevadans and tourists to make  responsible decisions  i'd like to recall what i did say on  march 18  just a year ago in response to the  governor's shutdown directive  and i quote this exactly  it has been my intent as the mayor of  this great city of las vegas  that we would be able to remain open for  business  even when realizing that there could  have been  constraints put upon us to which we  would have  reasonably adhered because  not only do i understand but also  because i'm  painfully aware and sensitive to the  very many who live  paycheck to paycheck i know we  and they cannot survive any total  shutdown of the economy  for any length of time beyond the  immediate week or two  so many working in hospital in the  hospitality industry  more likely in big hotels but also  those mom-and-pops small privately owned  businesses  these are most definitely at the  greatest  risk they cannot survive any lengthy  shutdown  and thus my full-out efforts will be  focused on keeping as many of  our people as possible employed  and asking our governor to  shorten the projected shutdown  and quote that was  a year ago here we are  a full year later our businesses are  still  only operating at 50 percent capacity  up from a bizarre 35 percent  that was effective until three days ago  some have not yet been permitted to open  at all our children are now  only returning part-time  to public school in a hybrid model  and then only kindergarten through fifth  in person  full-time on april 6th  tens of thousands of students have  missed out on graduation  proms extracurriculars sports  scholarship  not to mention a year's worth of  invaluable in-person instruction  in march 2020 when the governor  announced  in a quote and this is a quote a  courtesy call  that he was shutting the schools down i  pleaded with him  to implement safety measures and  mandatory temperature checks  instead for all entering the buildings  i was harshly told he was not seeking  any input  there is a mantra in some circle that  these draconians shut down  saved lives and while  any one death is beyond heartbreaking  the data shows no consistent  no consistent correlation in  death rates between states with  prolonged complete  shutdowns like nevada and those  that adopted more moderate safety  precautions  in fact the four states with the highest  death rates  were the states that adopted stringent  shutdown policies  one must also ask if masks  and social distancing are sufficient  now to slowing the spread of this  virus would that not have been  sufficient a full year ago  what is the rationale for continuing  even at 50 capacity  with other precautions like mass  mandates in place  in addition to increasing vaccinations  america is the land of the free but  americans in some states not all have  been forced to subjugate their freedoms  to the will of a single individual  seemingly in perpetuity there is  no apparent sunset on  emergency powers bestowed to some  governors  which smacks of tyranny  i am now calling for a return  to personal responsibility and personal  liberty those who do not want  to or choose to go out in public pace  places are not forced to do so  just as those who do not want the  vaccine  are not forced to take them  those who want to wear a mask or two or  three of them  are not prevented from wearing them  masks distancing frequent hand washing  and sanitation  are reasonable measures that health  officials assure  us truly make a difference  that is following the science  the science has not proven that  completely shutting down accomplished  anything more than moderate reasonable  precautions nevadans and americans are  smart enough to understand what's at  stake  and make appropriate choices for  themselves and their families  as one caller to my office recently  expressed  it is beyond sad and concerning  to see lady liberty on our las vegas  strip  wearing a mask it is the antithesis  of what she and america represent  personal freedom i said this a full year  ago tomorrow and i repeat it again  today the city of las vegas will seek  ways for  people and businesses to advocate for  their own lives  make their own choices create and follow  their  own destinies and live being assured  they have the right to do so in dignity  earning a livelihood providing for their  families and even helping others  to enjoy those same rights and dignities  upon these american founding  principles we will continue  to stand thank you my dear council  persons
 

